Changelog: 10-10-2026 20:56:48

Release 0.1.0. Initial release

Changelog: 09-10-2026 22:59:08

README: only the app's name, what it does and its license, with a link to its chapter of the manual; the rest moved into the manual (docs/apps/bios-reader.md). The flashrom hint links to the manual's "Reading the BIOS flash chip" section.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 19:22:06

The app itself. It reads a BIOS flash image (firmware volumes, files and sections, LZMA-packed volumes, the AMI
NVRAM store with variable chains and StdDefaults, the SMBIOS version) and the setup screens in it (HII forms and
en-US strings, with their SuppressIf, GrayOutIf and DisableIf conditions), with its own parser in Python. The window
shows them like the BIOS setup screen: tabs, items with their values, help with value, default, options and where
each value is stored, and the hidden menus and items with the reason they are hidden. Without a dump it shows the
running board: the setup screens from a built-in table of BIOS P5.00 and the values of the UEFI variables Linux can
read (AmdSetup). "Read BIOS chip" reads the flash chip twice with flashrom (read-only, through pkexec) and opens the
dump; "Open dump" opens one made earlier. A badge says whether the BIOS is stock: from a dump by comparing its
setup screens with those of stock P5.00, otherwise from the version string and the size of AmdSetup. The installer
keeps the dumps on uninstall unless --purge is given. --build-table makes the table of a stock release from a dump.
The logo is a placeholder.

Changelog: 09-10-2026 18:58:03

New app bios-reader: reads the BIOS settings of the BC-250 and shows them like the BIOS setup screen. The README
explains where the settings are stored, how to read the flash chip with flashrom (read-only) and how to unpack a
dump.
